  "name": {
    "en": "A2 Miloš Veliki Motorway (Belgrade – Preljina)"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "The A2 «Miloš Veliki» motorway on European route E763, running south-west from Belgrade at Surčin through Obrenovac, Ub, Lajkovac and Ljig to Preljina near Čačak, opened section by section between 2014 and 2019. Section lengths here are the figures published by JP Putevi Srbije rather than measurements off the mapped alignment: the Lajkovac–Ljig contract boundary sits about 3 km from the Ljig interchange used to cut the geometry, though the Lajkovac–Preljina total agrees to within 600 m. The motorway continues beyond Preljina toward Požega via Pakovraće and Lučani, and on to the planned Požega–Boljare extension; neither is recorded here for want of sourced opening dates."
  },
